Yes, I am running OpenVMS 7.2 on a Multia.

> Are there references that someone can point me to, pitfalls
> that I should be aware of, etc.?  Thanks.

Look up the section on MULTIA in the OpenVMS FAQ that can be found from a
link from http://www.openvms.compaq.com .

This will refer you to some supplemental information, and to the OpenVMS
freeware files that you will need.  The directions at the freeware site must
be followed.

In addition to the DOS floppy that you will need, and the ODS-2 formatted
floppy that you will need, I recommend that you create a second ODS-2
formatted floppy that contains the hobby license key command files, so that
you can license your machine fast and easily.

Be sure to read all the warnings about Multia heat-death.

