  serial connection and associated pinouts.

http://www.partner.compaq.com:9003/public/cheat_sheets/cables/padapters.html

  In the systems of this vintage, one of the following two pinouts 
  (straight-through and null-modem/cross-over, respectively) worked 
  with just about every serial widget, host, and modem that was then 
  in existence:


  1-------1
  2-------2
  3-------3
  4--+  +-4      4-----5
     |  |    or
  5--+  +-5      5-----4
  7-------7
  6--+
     |
  8--+---20
       +--6
       |
  20---+--8



  1-------1
  2-------3
  3-------2
  4--+  +-4      4-----5
     |  |    or
  5--+  +-5      5-----4
  7-------7
  6--+
     |
  8--+---20
       +--6
       |
  20---+--8



  Pins 4-5 and 5-4 are wired together only if hardware handshaking is 
  required, and the VAX-11/750 and the VT220 and most other systems
  of this vintage will use XON/XOFF flow control.


  Pin definitions:
    1  gnd
    2  txd (or rxd)
    3  rxd (or txd)
    4  cts
    5  rts
    6  dsr
    7  gnd
    8  dcd
    20 dtr


 --------------------------- pure personal opinion ---------------------------
   Hoff (Stephen) Hoffman   OpenVMS Engineering   hoffman#xdelta.zko.dec.com




