  involves an unsupported configuration -- often graphics other than the 
  (required) Qvision module (running at 1024 by 768 at 72 Hz) are not 
  compatible with the console, and will result in no power-up messages
  being displayed.

  Oh, and don't bother trying to extend the internal SCSI bus outside of 
  the box.  If you want an external SCSI, you will need a second SCSI
  controller, and all SCSI controllers must have the appropriate ROM
  revision (Adaptec 1740 or Adaptec 1742 with revision G.1, IIRC) for 
  use with OpenVMS (Hobbyist or otherwise)...

 --------------------------- pure personal opinion ---------------------------
   Hoff (Stephen) Hoffman   OpenVMS Engineering   hoffman#xdelta.zko.dec.com




