Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec
X-Complaints-To: abuse@rcn.com

If you don't see the usual C2032 or similar circular silver-colored
battery, or an obvious external battery, chances are the battery is
either a Dallas 12887 or a Benchmarq 3287.  Either one is a small
(~1.25"x0.75"x0.5") black rectangular intergrated circuit with CMOS,
clock, battery all rolled into one.  It is socketed, and can be easily
removed, but you'd have to get the specs for the battery to see which
pins to short out to clear the CMOS (and wipe out the BIOS password).
Far easier to look for a CMOS clear jumper on the main logic board
(DEC's term for motherboard, as known by the rest of the free world).

... Ben Myers

