:I'm in need of a SCSI disk controller for a VAX 6000-410.

  What I/O or storage bus(es) do you have available?
  Do you need boot support?
  What SCSI widget?

  The usual approaches for this class of system were via a KFMSA (XMI to 
  DSSI) and HSD-series (DSSI to SCSI) controller, or via served access to 
  a system with SCSI access (InfoServer, another cluster member), or via 
  a CIXCD (XMI to CI) and HSJ-series (CI to SCSI) controller.  

  There might be a third-party XMI to SCSI widget around somewhere, but 
  comparatively few third-party BI or XMI widgets exist, and I know of
  no XMI to SCSI module with support for OpenVMS VAX.

  There might well be a few other options available, if you have a BI or 
  a UNIBUS around...

