In article <3974BBFF.BC8BB8B9@mediaone.net>, 
Keith Mannisto <mannisto@mediaone.net> writes:

> What is this "m3119-ya" module?  Other markings on the board are
> "cxy08-m".
> Is it a SCSI quad/q-bus board?

No, it is an eight-port RS-232 serial controller with full
modem control on all eight lines.   It emulates the DEC
DHV11 or DHU11.

> If so, can it be used in a VAX-3800?  (So far, I know it fit into the
> system).

Yes, it can.

> If any one can provide this information or point me to a resource, it
> would be most appreciated.

DEC part numbers:

  EK-CXY08-IN   CXY08-AF 8-Line Asynchronous Multiplexer Option
                Installation Guide (~40 pages)

  EK-CXY08-TM   CXY08 Technical Manual (~150 pages)

  BC19N-12      Two 4-channel splitter cables

