If you have not alredy done so, please get and read the Upgrade and
Installation Guide.  This may answer some of your questions.

Your best option is probably to beg, borrow or by a CD reader.

OpenVMS VAX V7.2 is also available on TK50s and open reel tape.

If this is a new installation you will need either a CD or a TK50 drive
so that you can boot Standalone Backup.  Or, if you have an InfoServer, 
it can serve the CD and you can oot the CD via the InfoServer.

If you have multiple disks and you can make an image copy of the CD onto
one of the disks, you can then boot that disk as if it were the CD.
(Assumes another sytem on which this can be done.)

If this is an UPGRADE, you can copy the savsets into the [000000]
on your system disk (or another local disk) and upgrade from there.

