You don't, redhat won't run on that alpha. NetBSD runs fine though I
recently installed on a 400 connected to my hub with a 3000 300 floppy
temporary connected to the scsi bus. (boot 2 diskettes) Then remove the
floppy later.

Otherwise you could use bootp to install from a server but I'm not having
a lot of luck with bootp these days. (theory)

As for the console of the 400 (you can't use the normal display adapter
with netbsd no support) use the system console by plugging a DECnet MMJ
(like phone jack but tab is to the side) to a serial adapter plug on a PC
or terminal. So both your keyboard and display will be through a terminal
emulator.

Don't use the 25pin serial on the 400 it won't work for the console.

Hope this helps
-Walt

