Can someone clear up my confusion?

I understand that Workstations MARKETED for NT are designated as "a"-series
(e.g. PWS433a) and Unix/OpenVMS systems are designated as the "au"series
(e.g. PWS433au). I have been told that to convert an "a" system to an "au"
system is very difficult or even impossible without "secret" knowledge.
However, after reading postings here, I am starting to suspect that the only
thing required is to download and update the firmware. Of course, there are
other hardware dependencies, such as ensuring that there are OpenVMS drivers
for the video and scsi controller etc. in the system. But is this true, i.e.
the only difference is the firmware (which is tricky, but relatively easily
changed)?

I want to build up an OpenVMS 7.x system using hobbyist licenses. The "a"
series appear to be more widely available, but I  don't want to waste my
money on a system that cannot be converted.

Jon






