I started with a 433a with NT loaded.  I wanted Tru64.

Updated the Firmware to newest version.  There was a trick in changing from
alphabios to SRM.  You go into Setup, CMOS, hit F6 for advanced, then select
which firmware console you want to boot into.  F10 twice, exit, power down.
Power up and you are in SRM.

Before you do that you want to make sure you have SCSI and Video cards that
SRM will recognize.  I checked with DECpaq on the phone.  These two would
have cost me somewhere around $800 for parts from them.  I found that any
old S3 Trio chipset would work fine for X & CDE.  I found one on eBay and
paid a whopping $15 for it.   And that an old PCI Scsi card I had already
laying around with SC875 chipset worked fine and was supported by SRM and by
T64.

NET:  I had much much more time invested trying to dig out this information
than I had money invested in it.

Good luck.
Tom

