All of the information I can dig up on this laptop indicates that
the drive itself is a standard 'laptop' IDE disk.  (I haven't
seen the inside of this model, but all of the other Digital
Laptops I've worked on, including the HiNote VP, use standard
disk drives).

I did find a note that indicates that the BIOS will not support
a drive larger than 8.4 GB, so you should probably try to
use a disk no larger than this.

The following web site should be accessible, and it contains
the support files for the Ultra 2000

http://www4.support.compaq.com/support_database/index/epid75.htm

If you can't get to that try the Compaq home page and follow
the links for support.  The files for all of the old Digital
PCs should still be accessible.


