What version of VMS are you using?

For VMS 5.5-2, this is characteristic of a drive that has the AWRE
and/or ARRE (?) bits set incorrectly.  As was mentioned in a previous
post, you need to use a program to edit the SCSI mode pages to set these
bits correctly.

Good luck!

FWIW: Later versions of VMS are more tolerant of these bits.  I think
the change occured at VMS 6.2.
