>What version of VMS are you using?
>
>For VMS 5.5-2, this is characteristic of a drive that has the AWRE
>and/or ARRE (?) bits set incorrectly.  As was mentioned in a previous
>post, you need to use a program to edit the SCSI mode pages to set these
>bits correctly.
>
>Good luck!
>
>FWIW: Later versions of VMS are more tolerant of these bits.  I think
>the change occured at VMS 6.2.

That sounds about right.  But they are not in VMS 7.0 which came out
before 6.2 as I remember.  I have a DEC 3000 m400 here running 7.0.
With AWRE and ARRE enabled on a Seagate drive that was used to replace
a RZ26 system disk, we were able to load the disk but it was corrupted
very soon after.  Once they were disabled, the drive has worked well
for 2+ years since then.

