>
>Will the 50 to 68pin cable provide the correct pin termination to
>allow the disk to operate as a narrow (8-bit) device?

It should work OK, depending on the cable or the drive.  I don't know
about the cable, but do know that the 68-50 pin adapters can be found
with high-bit termination and without.  Some wide drives can be set to
terminate the high bits internally for you and just appear as a narrow
device.  You would have to check the specs for the drive you have.  I
do not remember if you said this drive was going to be system disk, if
so it would have to be under 1 GB.  As a data disk it should be fine
larger.  You may need to turn off the ARRE and AWRE settings in the
disk mode pages, depends on which version of the OS you will be running
on the 3100.  There are some utilities around to do that, I just attach
a drive to my Mac and use formatting software there to modify the mode
page settings.

Joe Heimann

