I had the same problem recently (fan fault indicator eliminated). You need
need to take off the front panel supporting bracket at the top, then take off 
the front panel, so that you can turn it up side down to take off the stand
to access the fans. Once you identified which fan is faulty, don't assume
it was the fan, because in my case it was a bad connection in the power supply 
itself (seperate feed per fan!!).  I couldn't get the power supply out, so that 
I could look at the connections, so I jumped the working supply to another fan 
to the fan that was not working (kept the same sensor connection (blue wire
though!!! Anyway the fist thing to do is swap round the fans to prove it's
a fan fault!
           By the way a Compaq engineer told me that many NIDEC fans dated 
1998 for this part no. (12-23609-12) were faulty.

Dave




