John:

Multia's do not have a removable graphics card.  The 8 plane TGA graphics
card is built in to the motherboard.
At the best you can add a second graphics adapter if your system has the
SCSI riser card with a PCI slot.
This card only came on VX41 & VX42's, and was a rather highly priced
option.  You can buy the riser card from Starship Corp, but they were a
little expensive as I recall.
If you have the riser card, I would expect that a S3 Virge or perhaps one
of the high end Matrox cards will work.  Have a look at what is legacy
supported in a newer Alpha and that will tell you what is supported in
the firmware.

Good luck!!

Tom Crabtree
