optional video has been found but its testing has not been started.
This is part of the console determination code."

Or to put it another way, it's tested ROM, NVR (non-volatile RAM), and
DZ, and is thinking of doing the video. The manual suggests removing
modules one at a time in order MSC (mass storage controller), graphics,
and memory. Having removed the graphics board you can set S3 to up and
plug a 9600 baud terminal into the printer port to see if it anything
more meaningful appears there.

It says a lot more than that, and yes, I have read a previous request
to type out and post the whole of Appendix G of the VS 3100 Maintenance
Guide (EK-285AA-MG-001), but as a former colleague used to say when
asked for product improvements: "will be considered, no action yet" :-)

Before delving inside the machine, I'd recommend the S3/terminal
approach (if you haven't already).

Chris



