I was once a Product Engineer in Manufactruing for the InfoServer product
set.

We made 3 types.

InfoServer 100 - Same as a MV3100 Model 20, different EPROM's.
InfoServer 150 - Similar to MV3100 Model 10e, different EPROM's and we
removed the floating point chip and various logic.
InfoServer 1000 - Not similar to anything, uses a CVAX chip, had everything
loaded into EPROM and EEROM.

Out of all the above, the InfoServer 100 could be converted to a MV3100 by
playing with the EPROM.

MV3100 Model 10, 10e, 20 and 20e could all be made into InfoServer 100 by
playing with EPROM.

That's it folks, trust me, OpenVMS has no clue about InfoServers, for
starters, they can't even create a valid HWRPB, and without that, OpenVMS
cannot figure out what the machine is.

InfoServer spoke MOP, LAD, LAST, no DECnet and no TCP/IP.





