    I'm fairly certain that it is neither, It's just plain ole' SCSI
("SCSI-1"), probably an NCR 53C80 Dual channel SCSI board. Unless you have a
DEC BC09J-xx or BC56H-xx SCSI cable, it might not work. Did you remove the
three terminating resistors on the SCSI board inside the case next to the
SCSI connector? Generally speaking you want both Term. Power and Term. Bus
power enabled, and in this case the terminating resistor packs installed on
the drive if it has them.

    Chris 




